{"name": "Batrachotomus", "clade": "loricata", "isd": false, "isnote": "", "sum": "Batrachotomus is a large loricatan pseudosuchian of the Middle Triassic of southern Germany with paired bony plates along its back.", "wsnote": "Wikipedia gives a 50 cm skull and a 47.8 cm femur for the holotype; no body-length estimate is given in the sources consulted, so these numbers are placeholders to check.", "holotype": "SMNS 52970, an almost complete skull and partial postcranial skeleton, the largest known specimen.", "material": "The holotype plus other specimens from the Erfurt Formation near Kupferzell, Germany.", "completeness": "multiple", "exceptional": "", "biology": "It lived in a swampy region; a series of small paired plates was attached to each vertebra, and a bone histology study has been made (Klein et al. 2017).", "author": "Gower 1999", "fad": 239.48, "lad": 237, "early": "Ladinian", "late": "", "type_species": "Batrachotomus kupferzellensis", "pbdb_occ": 3, "species": [{"name": "Batrachotomus kupferzellensis", "author": "Gower 1999", "fad": 239.48, "lad": 237, "interval": "Ladinian", "ref": "original description"}], "formations": [{"ids": ["erfurt-germany"], "formation": "Erfurt", "group": "Keuper", "members": ["Upper Lettenkeuper"], "country": "Germany", "regions": ["Baden-Württemberg"], "interval": "Longobardian", "n": 3, "ma": [237.0, 239.48]}], "images": [{"kind": "life", "file": "Batrachotomus kupferzellensis 2.JPG", "src": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Batrachotomus_kupferzellensis_2.JPG/960px-Batrachotomus_kupferzellensis_2.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batrachotomus_kupferzellensis_2.JPG", "artist": "Ghedoghedo", "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "licurl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0", "date": "Aug 2010 -", "caption": "Life restoration of Batrachotomus kupferzellensis.", "w": 2118, "h": 1406, "local": null, "r